<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Principality of Lucca and Piombino</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1805–1814</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Principality of Lucca and Piombino was a Napoleonic state in Tuscany created in 1805 for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s sister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elisa-bonaparte">Elisa Bonaparte</a> and her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/felice-baciocchi">Felice Baciocchi</a>. It replaced the old Republic of Lucca and absorbed the Principality of Piombino. Elisa reformed its administration and promoted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carrara">Carrara</a> marble, and the state ended with Napoleon's fall in 1814.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/principality-of-lucca-and-piombino.jpg" alt="Principality of Lucca and Piombino" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hierakares · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Principality_of_Lucca_(1805-1809).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
